{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4e3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b35b-88f7-7bd3-919f-b2bdc0ab1b29"},"sequence":204,"recorded_at":1780531400000403,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a38d6ec3-6f22-47d0-b372-c6eb68d9c789","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a38d6ec3-6f22-47d0-b372-c6eb68d9c789","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a38d6ec3-6f22-47d0-b372-c6eb68d9c789"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b35c-0bb0-7861-8c86-e1a5365f7739"},"task_id":"01a0b35c-0bb0-7861-8c86-e1a5365f7739","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b35c-0bb0-7861-8c86-e1a5365f7739","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-kkh1an/TASK-260830-kkh1an_reviewer-cr4.md`.\n1|Independently review Change Request revision 4 of TASK-260830-kkh1an (implement-terminal-instance-state-machine, the SECOND leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe ax-pane-and-terminal-instance-binding; the final leaf TASK-260830-2056mm follows; task_delta on the Story branch (trunk base c3aae73; checkpointed predecessors c61fc06 ; tip c61fc06ad8190a73c3005e137282829936dac970), published by RUN-260918-9edf2c on muse-spark max, 44 changed paths, patch and validation log attached as TASK-260830-kkh1an_change-request_rev4.patch / _rev4-validation.log. Revisions 1..3 are earlier construction attempts of the same producer scope that failed the Change Request validation suite on the pre-PR51 10m race-test timeout under concurrent suites; they carry no review verdict and no prior review findings — review revision 4 on its own merits.). Read the producer brief TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer.md, the outcome TASK-260830-kkh1an_results.md, TASK-260830-kkh1an_conformance-matrix.md, TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer-evidence.tar.gz, the predecessor's accepted evidence (TASK-260830-1geqhj_results.md and its verdict TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-verdict-rev4.md, accepted by RUN-260917-e644e0 with no P1 and no P2), the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. The normative authority is the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md Section 4.C (Lifecycle and operations) with 4.B, 4.D, 5.2 and 7.A as its context. The landed owner being extended is internal/terminalbackend, which already holds InstanceState/ParseInstanceState, Operation/ParseOperation, SideEffect/ParseSideEffect, Transition/CheckTransition, CheckErrorAllowed, IdempotencyKey, Receipt/Ledger/ImportLedger, StatusResult/CheckStatusResult and AttachAuthorization — a second state machine or a second enum is a P1, not a style note.\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments. (0) REWORK VERIFICATION FIRST — revision 3 was routed CHANGES REQUESTED by RUN-260918-f6b44c with NO P1 and with most of the leaf CONFIRMED by that reviewer's own instruments (F1's same-key retry after status meeting the behavioural bar at both seams under real SIGKILLs, F2's remote-winner arms fencing through the landed gate, E1's create-row gates, E2's third-position rechecks and session axis all pinned with their mutants dying, the shipped harness 100/100 twice, the ratio re-derived to 84 of 84, the full suite green, hygiene clean). Two findings remained and BOTH were marked `repeat-of` the round before: F3 — ObserveFencing still never fenced a stale incarnation whose observation carries NO live fencing grant (the lapsed-grant and no-grant/controller-restart members of the cold force takeover, under a local and a remote winner alike), because a grant authorizes but does not make an incarnation less stale; the sanctioned fix lands an exported staleness verdict in internal/fencing that decides direction and tuple arms over a verified well-formed winner WITHOUT the grant precondition, and the alternative — declaring fencing observation grant-gated — is legitimate only if doc.go, TRACEABILITY and the README say so and name the recovery route the final leaf owes. E3 — the per-effect authorization recheck was pinned on the lease-tuple axis only, so an authorization EXPIRING between effects committed the remaining effects with the whole suite green under a one-line mutant. Read TASK-260830-kkh1an_review-verdict-rev3.md and its evidence archive. Grade both findings as a CLASS, not as the witnessed members: enumerate the members yourself (grant present / lapsed / absent, crossed with local and remote winner, from active, parked and quiescing) and check each is either driven or excluded by a stated bound, since this leaf has now shipped a members-only fix twice on these same two classes. Confirm the internal/fencing change is confined to the exported verdict and restructures nothing else there, and that a harness row exists which keeps the tuple recheck while dropping the expiry recheck. Then proceed to your own independent review of the whole revision: (1) Spec fidelity — extract Section 4.C yourself and diff it against the candidate: the eight-state closed enum, the closed TerminalBackendSideEffect / PresentationTransport / ProviderProofKind / TerminalStatusLastEffect vocabularies, the AXAuthorization member set with the epoch bound witnessed at 1, 9007199254740991 and both adjacent out-of-range values, and the RetryDisposition enum (replay_same, status_first, new_authorization, required_operator_action) carried by every result. Assert the LITERAL spec tokens, not the package's own constants — a test comparing a value against the constant that produces it pins nothing, and a same-exit value swap is the plant that proves it. (2) The state-entry rules, each driven and each mutated: `creating` entered only by `create`, only after the durable idempotency receipt and before the first side effect; an error BEFORE a side effect restoring the source state; an error AFTER an unprovable effect moving to `unavailable` with `status_first` and never claiming `absent`; only `quiesce-input` entering `quiescing`; no backend operation entering `stale_fenced` (AX fencing observation does, through the landed internal/fencing projection — check it is composed, not re-implemented); authorization AND generation rechecked immediately before EACH side effect rather than once at entry; a deadline cancelling waiting but never a committed effect. (3) Generation-safe evidence — `backend_generation` is the canonical string[1..256] bound in every containing contract: witness 0 and 257 refused and 256 accepted in the Binding, the Provider Protocol 3 descriptor, every operation body and the CLI Result 4 summary projection, and confirm a stale generation refuses with the landed `terminal_backend_stale_generation` rather than a fresh code. (4) The operation rows for status, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary and request-stop: exact source→target states, the listed side effects, the exact idempotency key material (the UTF-8 concatenations the spec spells out), the evidence kinds, and the exact admitted refusal sets — a code outside a row's set must be rejected by `CheckErrorAllowed`, and `status` timeout or read failure must be `unknown`, never `absent`. (5) Crash and idempotency — rerun the producer's real-kill tests twice, inject your own crash at the receipt seam, and confirm an identical retry replays while a changed operation in-window is `idempotency_mismatch`. (6) Mutation — rerun the shipped harness in an isolated copy, rerun each KILLED twice, and plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on arms the producer did not mutate (one recheck dropped, one bound widened by one, one disposition mapping collapsed, one closed-enum member admitted) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (7) Bounds and hygiene — no `ax` CLI, no tmux/ConPTY process control, no provider process; internal/traceability untouched (the final leaf owns the registry); the candidate byte-identical to trunk everywhere outside this Story's scope; README additive with no capability claim; gofmt/vet clean; the full configured suite green on the exact tree.\n4|\n5|Method: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every harness; keep scratch small under .temp/TASK-260830-kkh1an/ and delete candidate copies when done. Report the coverage ratio YOU measured against the acceptance table's real row count, not the producer's restated one. Attach TASK-260830-kkh1an_review-verdict-rev4.md and TASK-260830-kkh1an_review-evidence-rev4.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260830-kkh1an, revision=4, evidence=TASK-260830-kkh1an_review-verdict-rev4.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named and a short \"Rework scope (for the producer)\" section at the end. Model: claude-opus-5 max. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","final_result":true}}}
